{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["Spices — I have already explained it above." "Spices and pure frankincense — according to the plain sense: at first it states a general category: Take you spices — and then specifies what the spices are: נטף and שחלת and חלבנה — these are the spices that I commanded you to take. And further take — and pure frankincense — according to the plain sense: pure frankincense is not 'spices,' and it is other than the first 'spices' that were in the verse. Thus too is the way of verses: to state a general category and then specify, and then go back and say: here is the general category I stated to you. So too regarding Noah: ויאמר אלהים אל נח זאת אות הברית אשר הקימותי וגו׳."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:43:40.541474177Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}